            <div class="msg msg-user"><p>How should I use tasks?</p></div>
            <div class="msg msg-agent">
              <p>Stop treating threads as tasks. Your job is a clear vision of what to build. That’s it.</p>
              <ol class="step-list">
                <li>Open a thread</li>
                <li>Talk the idea through with me</li>
                <li>Ask me to create a task for a worker</li>
                <li>While it runs, explore the next idea and queue a task for that too</li>
                <li>Repeat until the workers have enough work, then walk away</li>
                <li>Task statuses show up as clickable badges on the thread in the sidebar</li>
                <li>Next time you open your computer, ask me what got done. I’ll have everything that needs your attention ready in this thread. You tell me what to refine or what’s next.</li>
              </ol>
            </div>
            <!-- data-pause: extra reading room before this message (story.ts). -->
            <div class="msg msg-user" data-pause>
              <p>Okay. Let’s add a compact sidebar to Up.computer.</p>
            </div>
            <div class="msg msg-agent">
              <p>I’ll create a UI developer worker on Claude Opus 5.5 and give it the task. Want Codex 6.2 Astra to review it when it’s done?</p>
              <div class="card agent-card">
                <span class="card-icon"><Fragment set:html={svg("bot")} /></span>
                <span class="card-main"><strong>UI developer</strong><small>Worker · Claude Opus 5.5 · one task at a time</small></span>
